<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nawrahta Minsaw</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1551">1551</a>–<a href="/years/1607">1607</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nawrahta Minsaw was a son of the Burmese king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayinnaung">Bayinnaung</a> who ruled Lan Na as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> king from 1579 to 1607, replacing the native line of rulers. After his father's empire broke up he governed Chiang Mai largely independently, and he is remembered as a patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> and of Lan Na literature.</p></div>
